@page "/"

<PageTitle>Home — Authentication State</PageTitle>

<div style="padding: 2rem;">

    <div class="hero-section">
        <div style="position:relative; z-index:1;">
            <div style="font-size:0.8rem; font-weight:700; letter-spacing:1px; opacity:0.75; text-transform:uppercase; margin-bottom:0.5rem;">
                Visual Programming · Lab 04
            </div>
            <h1>Application 05</h1>
            <p>Authentication State — Service-Based Login with State Change Events</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row g-3 mb-4">

        <div class="col-md-4">
            <div class="feature-card rose">
                <div class="feature-icon">🎯</div>
                <h5>Objective</h5>
                <p>Simulate authentication state using a Singleton service with event-driven UI updates.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="col-md-4">
            <div class="feature-card green">
                <div class="feature-icon">⚙️</div>
                <h5>Technologies</h5>
                <p>Blazor Server, DI Singleton, <code>Action</code> events, <code>IDisposable</code>.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="col-md-4">
            <div class="feature-card amber">
                <div class="feature-icon">✨</div>
                <h5>Features</h5>
                <p>Live sidebar auth indicator, animated login/logout, profile page with access control.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

    </div>

    <div class="info-badge">
        <span style="font-size:1.3rem;">📘</span>
        <span>
            <strong>Student Assignment Project</strong> — Demonstrates shared state management across Blazor components.
        </span>
    </div>

</div>